  "function_translated_nl": "Lesson context: lesson_05. Let triangle ABC be a triangle with sides AB = 14, BC = 16, AC = 10. Let triangle MNP be a triangle. Let segment MN be a midsegment segment. Let segment NP be a midsegment segment. Let segment MP be a midsegment segment. Let point M be a point on AB. Let point N be a point on BC. Let point P be a point on AC. Segment MN is parallel to AC. Segment NP is parallel to AB. Segment MP is parallel to BC. Find the length of MN.",
  "student_facing_prose": "A triangular plot of land ABC has sides measuring AB = 14 meters, BC = 16 meters, and AC = 10 meters. A surveyor marks three points\u2014M on side AB, N on side BC, and P on side AC\u2014each at the midpoint of its respective side. She then draws segments connecting these midpoints to form triangle MNP inside the original triangle.\n\nBecause M and N are midpoints, the segment MN is parallel to the third side AC. Similarly, because N and P are midpoints, segment NP is parallel to AB. And because M and P are midpoints, segment MP is parallel to BC.\n\nThe surveyor knows that triangle MNP is a dilation of triangle ABC with center at vertex A and scale factor 1/2 (since the midpoints are half the distance from A along each side). This means the sides of the inner triangle are half the length of the corresponding sides of the outer triangle.\n\nWhat is the length of segment MN?"
}